From 489056185e13eb28897a81f3f8d9cec3528b6e6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 3 <phase3@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:13:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] RISC-V: match WCH fast-interrupt vector saves

WCH fast interrupt handlers do not software-save vector registers by
default.  The existing frame logic instead treated them like ordinary
functions and emitted vlenb-based vector spills in four EVT projects.

Add the observed --param=ccv-abi= control as per-function optimization
state.  Its default and value zero suppress all fast-interrupt vector
software saves; value one preserves only live vector-ABI callee-saved
registers.  Cover the accepted range, default and explicit-zero behavior,
mixed live registers, and the nonleaf ABI save set.

The behavior comes from an official O0/O2/Os by unset/0/1 matrix, exact
option diagnostics, and an LTO-linked probe.  The four affected projects
now match 100/100 gate artifacts, the selected EVT gate remains 274/274,
and all 30279 PASS tuples of the RC04 (mret repair round) RISC-V suite
baseline remain PASS.

Behavior evidence:
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t3-rc05/probe-compare-final
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t3-rc05/cluster-run-final
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t3-rc05/suite-diff-riscv-final
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/t3-rc05/quick-gate-final
  tmp/phase3d-evidence/posthoc-rc05-darwin-full-stage-a

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* params.opt: Add --param=ccv-abi=.
	* config/riscv/riscv.cc (riscv_wch_fast_interrupt_saved_reg_p): Add
	the vector registers, honouring --param=ccv-abi=.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-vector-default.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-vector-param-range.c: New
	test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-vector-param0.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-vector-param1-nonleaf.c: New
	test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-fast-interrupt-vector-param1.c: New test.
